From 8b83c97778de7650377e539105fb7394e04c9bac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Rodriguez <chiva.boijr@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:15:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] vLLM for Windows 0.32.0 release

Windows support ported to the v0.32.0 release:
- Re-based the v0.31.0-era Windows patch (SystemPanic/vllm-windows 3b5b6bcac)
  onto the v0.32.0 tree.
- csrc: MSVC-compatible kernel fixes re-landed at the post-consolidation
  (PR #60721) paths; upstream's VLLM_STABLE_DISPATCH_BOOL dispatch kept,
  static-constexpr MSVC treatment preserved where applicable.
- Build: Windows guards in setup.py/CMakeLists/external project cmake kept;
  DeepGEMM uses the upstream TORCH_LIBRARY layout (abi3) with the Windows
  CUTLASS memory patch applied on WIN32; torch 2.13.0+cu132 Windows wheel
  now matches the upstream pin.
- Runtime: spawn-based multiprocessing, named shared-memory and signal
  handling fixes for Windows re-applied onto the v0.32.0 V1 worker/executor
  code.

Co-authored-by: OpenCode <opencode@local>
